                <pb facs="0527" n="507" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg507"/>

                <head>[Extract from synopsis, fourth paragraph. ]</head>
                <p>James McHugh, of Belfast, writes to Mr. Gray, asking him to use his influence
                    with Governor Brown to have a friend made paymaster on one of the confederate
                    men-of-war, and congratulating him on the defeat of Rosecrans; also telling him
                    to hold on to his bonds, as they will soon be at par, and as Mr. Gray is about
                    returning to the confederacy to return and bring out more bonds.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1863-10-02"><hi rendition="#small-caps">October</hi> 2,
                            1863</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
